-**Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-- **Large Scene Scale:** Large $L$ with standard initialization leads to large alpha values (opaque scene) because $d$ is large. This causes optimization failure due to dense floaters [S1].
-- **Initialization Scheme:** Using default PyTorch linear layer initialization for ReLU MLPs results in raw outputs with mean 0 and variance 0, causing random failure modes across all scaling factors $k$. Kaiming uniform initialization with $\sqrt{2}$ gain is recommended to correct for ReLU variance gain, resulting in a non-zero $\tau$ [S1].
-- **Activation Functions:** For ReLU and softplus activations, closed-form expressions for $\mu$ are not available. Instead, the offset is tuned numerically to achieve $\mathbb{E}[\sigma] \cdot L = \log(1/T')$ by shifting the activation function profile to the right (adding negative offset to input) [S1].
-- **Ray Length Variation:** For real-life scenes where ray length varies, a possible choice is to set $L$ to the longest ray distance [S1].
